#   D2b  classList.add/remove/toggle wrote the reflected className property and
#        NOT the sattr_ content-attribute store, which is the store
#        _el_get_attribute consults FIRST. setAttribute('class') had always
#        written both. So on a source-anchored element getAttribute('class')
#        and el.attributes answered the PARSE-TIME class forever.
#        Fixed in _cls_write_o — one writer, both stores.
#   D3   insertBefore(DocumentFragment, ref) inserted NOTHING. A fragment is
#        deliberately not a created-node-pool member, so _insert_before_v's
#        _find_cre_by_obj() test failed and the whole staged batch was dropped
#        on the floor. appendChild had had the spec's "insert the children,
#        leave the fragment empty" step since it was written; insertBefore
#        never got it.
#   D4   node.parentNode still named the old parent after removeChild(). TWO
#        causes, one per branch: the created-node branch never nulled it, and
#        the source branch nulled it BEFORE the child-list surgery — and that
#        surgery reads parent.children, a LAZY accessor that materialises the
#        subtree from the parse tree and re-writes parentNode on every child,
#        overwriting the null it had just written. NID_REMCHILD carried a
#        second copy of _remove_child_v; there is now one, and it unlinks
#        AFTER the wiring.
#   +    appendChild() of a SOURCE element was a total no-op (only created
#        nodes had a branch), so the remove+re-add every reconciler does left
